Do not inject tbbmalloc_proxy into the embedded Windows host.

tbbmalloc_proxy detours the CRT allocator process wide when the module is
loaded, before main() runs, and the forced __TBB_malloc_proxy reference makes
that happen for anything linking creator.cc. In the embedded Qt/Blender host
that detour crashes Windows startup. Blender's own executable keeps the proxy,
and the explicit scalable_allocator uses, including the GMP workaround below,
are untouched: only the process-wide interception is dropped, and only for
WITH_BTS_HOST, which native/host/CMakeLists.txt defines on the bts-host target
alone.

The same edit is made by scripts/cross-windows/prepare-cross.py for the
Linux-hosted cross build. Carrying it here as well gives the native MSVC path
in docs/building.md and the release workflow the same fix.

diff --git a/source/creator/creator.cc b/source/creator/creator.cc
--- a/source/creator/creator.cc
+++ b/source/creator/creator.cc
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 #  endif
 #endif
 
-#if defined(WITH_TBB_MALLOC) && defined(_MSC_VER) && defined(NDEBUG)
+#if defined(WITH_TBB_MALLOC) && defined(_MSC_VER) && defined(NDEBUG) && !defined(WITH_BTS_HOST)
 #  pragma comment(lib, "tbbmalloc_proxy.lib")
 #  pragma comment(linker, "/include:__TBB_malloc_proxy")
 #endif
